! ansys_p4_harm_ff_y_v2_h112_e31m_2026-09-24.inp
! e31 SIGN CLONE (2026-09-24, clone_e31m_decks_2026-09-24.py, LESSONS Sec 18.244).
! Parent: ansys_p4_harm_ff_y_v2_h112_2026-09-16.inp. Only changes: E31 = -4.1E-3 (Liu 2002 / Duan 2005
! Table 1 as printed) and every *CFOPEN output name + '_e31m'.
! Targets quoted in the parent header below are the OLD +4.1 values.
! Do not put the MAPDL failure token in this file.
! ansys_p4_ff_piezo_ring_2026-09-15.inp
! Paper 4 (piezoelectric ring) -- first FE cross-check deck for the F-F
! (free-free) piezo-coupled LAYERED annular ring, p=0 (axisymmetric),
! h1/2h=1/12. Written 2026-09-15, same session as LESSONS_LEARNED.md
! Sec 18.149 (F-F derivation + validation) and the sibling scripts
! probe_piezo_p4_ff_forward_model_2026-09-15.py /
! probe_piezo_p4_elastic_ff_baseline_2026-09-15.py.
!
! ============================================================
!
! ============================================================
! UNITS RESCALE (2026-09-16), following LESSONS_LEARNED.md Sec 18.161's
! "next concrete step, not yet attempted": a from-scratch, validated,
! consistent unit-system rescale of the whole piezo deck family, to
! shrink the ~20-order-of-magnitude spread between the mechanical block
! (order 1E9-1E13 in SI Pa-based units) and the electrical/piezoelectric
! block (permittivity order 1E-9 F/m) that five independent cheap-lever
! probes (jobs 2490482, 2490571/2490582, 2490583) could not resolve.
!
! CHOSEN SYSTEM: mm - N - s - tonne (mechanical), REAL VOLTS (electrical
! potential unchanged). This is NOT an arbitrary or guessed choice -- it
! is the one non-SI system where the force unit N and the time unit s
! are UNCHANGED from SI (since tonne*mm/s^2 = 1000kg*1e-3m/s^2 = kg*m/s^2
! = N exactly), which is why frequencies (1/s) come out in real Hz with
! zero further conversion, and it is the standard "mm-N-s-tonne" system
! already ubiquitous in mm-scale FE work (ANSYS/LS-DYNA/Abaqus alike).
!
! DERIVATION (first principles, cross-checked 3 independent ways -- T-
! equation substitution, electromechanical energy-density bookkeeping,
! and base-unit/derived-charge-unit substitution -- all three agree):
!
!  length      L' = L[m] * 1000                      (m -> mm)
!  mass        M' = M[kg] * 1e-3                      (kg -> tonne;
!                                                       DERIVED, not
!                                                       independently
!                                                       chosen, from
!                                                       F=ma consistency)
!  density     rho' = rho[kg/m^3] * 1e-12             (kg/m^3 -> tonne/mm^3)
!  stress/     E' = E[Pa] * 1e-6                       (Pa -> MPa = N/mm^2;
!  modulus                                             an exact, always-
!                                                       valid physical
!                                                       unit conversion)
!  potential   V' = V[Volt]  (UNCHANGED -- our deliberate choice, so
!                              VOLT dof / D,ALL,VOLT,0 BCs stay literal,
!                              physical volts, no BC rewriting needed)
!  el. field   E_field'[V/mm] = E_field[V/m] * 1e-3   (implied by the
!                              geometry now being in mm; not a material
!                              constant, so nothing to type in directly)
!  ABS.        eps' = eps[F/m]  UNCHANGED NUMERICALLY. Proof: F/m, fully
!  PERMITTIVITY decomposed into base units, is F/m = (C^2/(N*m))/m =
!  (MP,PERx)   C^2/(N*m^2); substituting the SI identity C = N*m/V (from
!              V=J/C, J=N*m) gives C^2/(N*m^2) = N/V^2 -- the "m" cancels
!              EXACTLY, so absolute permittivity has NO net length
!              dependence once expressed in N and V (which are both
!              unchanged in this system) -- confirmed independently by
!              the energy-density route (T-form energy density (1/2)eps*
!              E^2 must equal (1/2)eps'*E'^2 once both are expressed in
!              the new energy-density unit MPa=mJ/mm^3, and E'=E*1e-3
!              exactly cancels the implied 1e-6 from Pa->MPa against
!              eps' = eps, i.e. no eps rescale needed).
!  PIEZO e-    e' = e[C/m^2] * 1e-3. Derived from the T-equation
!  CONSTANT    T = c:S - e^T:E: converting T and c from Pa to MPa (each
!  (TB,PIEZ,   x1e-6) and E from V/m to V/mm (x1e-3, i.e. E=E'*1e3),
!  TBDATA,     T'*1e6 = c'*1e6*S - e*(E'*1e3)  =>  T' = c'*S - (e*1e-3)*E'
!  stress form)  => e' = e*1e-3. Independently re-derived via the
!              charge-unit-substitution method (deriving the coherent
!              charge unit Q* implied by keeping real Volts and mJ=N*mm
!              energy, Q*=1e-3 C, then re-expressing C/m^2 in Q*/mm^2)
!              -- both methods agree exactly: e' = e[C/m^2] * 1e-3.
!  length      any PURE length tolerance (e.g. NUMMRG's node-merge
!  tolerance   distance) is rescaled x1000 like any other length, e.g.
!              1.0E-8 m -> 1.0E-5 mm.
!
! NOT hand-derived from an "empirical" ABAQUS-forum factor (the risk the
! session notes flagged) -- every factor above follows from ANSYS's own
! documented TB,PIEZ constitutive form (T=c:S-e^T:E, D=e:S+eps^S:E,
! stress-form default TBOPT, already independently confirmed correct in
! Sec 18.157) and ordinary SI dimensional analysis, not a borrowed number.
!
! VALIDATION STAGING (per the ground rules -- do NOT trust a coupled
! result in the new units before these pass): this submission batches
! the bare-host elastic-only deck and the piezo-coupling-off deck
! rescaled into these SAME units FIRST. Both are purely mechanical
! eigenvalue problems (piezo-coupling-off has e=0 everywhere, so its
! VOLT dof is present but completely decoupled from the mechanical
! modes) -- their frequencies are mathematically GUARANTEED invariant
! under any internally-consistent unit rescaling, so they are a real
! check on the ARITHMETIC of this conversion (did every E, rho, C_ij
! actually get rescaled correctly), not on the physics. Confirmation
! criteria: (a) rescaled bare-host mode 2 must reproduce 114.89 Hz
! (job 2490363's own result) to at least 4 significant figures -- NOT
! merely "close to 115.68 Hz", since a few-percent FE-discretization
! gap is expected and already characterized, but ANY unit-conversion
! arithmetic error would show up as a gap much larger than that
! already-known discretization error, or as a wildly wrong number; (b)
! rescaled piezo-coupling-off mode 2 must reproduce 118.81016 Hz (job
! 2490456's own result) to at least 4 significant figures, same
! reasoning. If EITHER fails, the units arithmetic (not the physics) is
! wrong and the FIX-v6-coupled result below must not be trusted.
!
! ONLY once (a) and (b) both pass does the coupled result below become
! trustworthy: mode 2 should land near 119.058 Hz (closed-form target)
! with a real O(0.1-1)-magnitude bending discriminator and the exact 0 Hz
! rigid-body mode should reappear, if the ~20-order-of-magnitude SI-units
! disparity really was the root cause of the catastrophic ill-
! conditioning (residual 4.15E+02 at full coupling, job 2490482).
! ============================================================
! WHY THIS DECK: no literature F-F piezo benchmark exists (LESSONS_LEARNED
! Sec 18.144 Finding 2 -- confirmed again, not re-litigated here), so FE is
! the ONLY external validation channel available for the F-F piezo-coupled
! forward model, per PAPER4_PIEZO_ROADMAP.md Sec 8 step 3. This is the
! layered-ring FE cross-check the C-C side never needed (C-C had Duan2005
! Table 4 to check against directly) and the disk smoke deck
! (ansys_piezo_disk_modal_plane223.inp) was NOT (monolithic disk, different
! geometry, no benchmark target either -- see that deck's own header).
!
! TARGET TO CHECK AGAINST: probe_piezo_p4_ff_forward_model_2026-09-15.py's
! own p=0, h1/2h=1/12 result: omega=747.9929 rad/s => f=119.058 Hz. This
! deck's job is to find a genuine FE flexural mode near that frequency, not
! to blindly trust whichever mode number happens to fall near it -- see the
! MODE-SHAPE DISCRIMINATOR note below, this matters because a layered
! axisymmetric solid mesh mixes flexural (bending) and extensional
! (breathing/radial) mode families in one spectrum, unlike the pure-
! bending Kirchhoff theory this project's own solver assumes.
!
! GEOMETRY: layered annular ring, R_i=0.1 m, R_o=0.6 m (Duan2005 Table 4's
! own target), steel host |z|<=h (h=0.01, Duan's own half-thickness
! symbol), PZT4 piezo layers bonded symmetrically on both faces,
! h<=z<=h+h1 and mirror -h-h1<=z<=-h, h1=2h/12 (Table-4 ratio 1/12).
! TRUE FREE-FREE: since R_i=0.1 > 0, the ring does NOT touch the axis of
! revolution, so (unlike the disk smoke deck, which needed UX=0 at r=0 to
! suppress the on-axis singularity) NO mechanical constraint is applied
! anywhere -- this is a genuinely unconstrained modal solve. Expect rigid-
! body translation (and, if p>0 were modeled, rotation) modes near f=0 Hz
! at the bottom of the spectrum; these are correct, not a bug (same
! precedent as the disk smoke deck's own mode-1-at-0-Hz note).
!
! ELEMENT/MATERIAL STRATEGY: ONE element type (PLANE223, KEYOPT(1)=1001,
! KEYOPT(3)=1 axisymmetric) used for BOTH the steel host AND the PZT4
! layers, with two different material IDs -- NOT two different element
! types -- specifically so the host/piezo interface line shares nodes
! naturally through ordinary area meshing (no manual node-merging step,
! no mismatched-DOF-set interface to debug). The steel material gets the
! piezoelectric (TB,PIEZ) terms all zero and a small nominal permittivity
! (not exactly zero -- an exactly-zero diagonal permittivity would leave
! VOLT undefined/singular at any node touching ONLY steel elements) so
! every node in the mesh carries a well-posed VOLT dof, even though VOLT
! is physically meaningless in the steel region (e=0 there, so it never
! couples to anything mechanical) -- this mirrors how coupled-field meshes
! with an inert region are conventionally built, not a project-specific
! trick.
!
! ELECTRICAL BC: DRIVEN 1 V (lever 9), not open-circuit and not
! both-faces SC. VOLT=0 on the host/piezo INTERFACE (z=+-h). Outer
! faces z=+-(h+h1) have D,VOLT,1.0 on every node (prescribed 1 V
! bus). Do not re-open mesh/units/TB,PIEZ.
!
! MODE-SHAPE DISCRIMINATOR (read the postprocessing section before
! trusting a specific mode number as "the" flexural mode): a genuine
! p=0 axisymmetric BENDING mode has UY (axial = out-of-plane transverse
! displacement, matching this project's w) nearly the SAME SIGN AND
! MAGNITUDE through the thickness at a given r (Kirchhoff kinematics:
! uz=w(r), no z-dependence), while UX (radial, in-plane) has OPPOSITE
! SIGN top vs bottom (bending strain ur=-z*dw/dr, linear in z, flips sign
! through the mid-plane). A "breathing"/extensional mode is the reverse:
! UX same sign top/bottom (uniform radial stretch), UY small/near-zero.
! The postprocessing block below prints UX and UY at matched top/bottom
! node pairs at the outer radius for every extracted mode specifically so
! this can be checked by eye against the printed table, rather than
! trusting mode order alone.
!
! STATUS (2026-09-15, UPDATED post-job-2490363 isolation test, FIX v4):
! FOUR runs of THIS deck so far (2489625, 2490219, 2490239 all byte-
! identical nonphysical; 2490350 confirmed the v3 mesh fix correct --
! piezo layers 80/80 elements, warnings 85->2 -- but frequency barely
! moved, 3427->3422 Hz, still ~29x off 119.058 Hz target). The only
! remaining non-routine warning in 2490350's log was ANSYS's own
! eigensolver ill-conditioning note. A SEPARATE bare-host isolation deck
! (ansys_p4_ff_bare_host_smoke_2026-09-15.inp, no piezo/VOLT coupling at
! all) then ran clean (job 2490363): 0 mesh warnings, NO ill-conditioning
! warning, mode 2 within 0.68% of its 115.68 Hz target, clean bending
! discriminator signature -- DECISIVELY ruling out geometry/meshing/
! free-free-BC as the cause and narrowing the search to THIS deck's own
! piezo coupled-field/permittivity setup. FIX v4 applied below: X_INERT
! raised from 1.0E-15 to 1.0E-9 (same order of magnitude as the real
! PZT4 X11/X33, not 6-7 orders below them) -- see the X_INERT definition
! itself and LESSONS_LEARNED.md Sec 18.154 for the full rationale and
! pre-registered confirmation criteria. NOT YET RE-RUN.
!
! STATUS UPDATE (2026-09-15, FIX v6, following the piezo-coupling-off
! isolation deck's DECISIVE PASS, job 2490456 -- LESSONS_LEARNED.md Sec
! 18.156): the elastic layered composite alone (TB,PIEZ,2 zeroed) lands
! at 118.81 Hz, 0.21% from the 119.058 Hz target -- conclusively
! implicating THIS material's TB,PIEZ,2 TBDATA block as the sole
! remaining cause. A from-scratch re-derivation of ANSYS's TB,PIEZ
! TBDATA convention (cross-checked against ANSYS's own coupled-field
! docs AND an independent forum-posted worked example for a Y-poled
! material, both agreeing exactly) found the convention is: 18 values,
! grouped by STRESS/STRAIN ROW (x,y,z,xy,yz,zx -- 6 groups of 3), each
! group cycling the electric FIELD column (X,Y,Z) fastest -- i.e.
! TBDATA index = (stress_row-1)*3 + field_col. This deck's PREVIOUS
! block (and the disk-smoke deck's, ansys_piezo_disk_modal_plane223.inp,
! it was copied from) instead filled TBDATA as if grouped by FIELD row
! (3 groups of 6, stress cycling fastest) -- the TRANSPOSE of ANSYS's
! actual matrix, an easy mistake for TB,PIEZ specifically since (unlike
! the symmetric TB,ANEL block, which this same deck gets right) the
! piezoelectric matrix is a non-square 6x3 and the row/column meaning
! is easy to invert. Read literally, the OLD block placed the response
! of the HOOP normal stress (row 3) to the RADIAL field (E31, should be
! exactly zero by transverse-isotropy symmetry) and to the POLING field
! (E33=14.1 instead of the correct E31=4.1, ~3.4x too large) -- while
! leaving ALL THREE of the physically dominant, active bending-relevant
! terms exactly zero: radial-normal-stress<->poling-field (E31, row 1),
! axial-normal-stress<->poling-field (E33, row 2), and the r-z bending
! shear<->radial-field term (E15, row 4, the only piezo term that
! directly couples to Kirchhoff-type bending shear). This fully accounts
! for a spurious, physically nonsensical dominant electromechanical term
! unrelated to true bending stiffness -- consistent with the observed
! ~29x frequency / ~840x apparent-stiffness anomaly, far beyond real
! PZT4 coupling factors (k^2~0.3-0.7). FIX v6 (below): TB,PIEZ,2's
! TBDATA rewritten to the verified-correct layout -- nonzero at
! positions 2 (E31), 5 (E33), 8 (E31), 10 (E15); position 15 (E15) is
! the second, symmetric shear term but is kinematically inert here (no
! hoop displacement DOF in this axisymmetric, non-torsion element, same
! as rows 5/6 already being inert per the Sec 18.156 manual audit).
! PRE-REGISTERED CONFIRMATION CRITERIA for the next run: (a) mode 2
! should land close to the 119.058 Hz closed-form target -- given the
! coupling-off baseline is already 118.81 Hz (0.21% off), the genuine
! coupling-induced shift should be small (a fraction of a percent, NOT
! a jump to/near 3422 Hz); (b) the discriminator should show the same
! clean bending signature as job 2490456 (UY_top~=UY_bot, UX_top~=-UX_bot)
! at that mode, not the 1E-10-to-1E-17 noise floor seen in every prior
! coupled run; (c) no ill-conditioning warning (X_INERT=1.0E-9, FIX v4,
! is untouched by this fix and was already only a partial, unrelated
! conditioning improvement -- see Sec 18.155). If (a)-(b) still fail,
! the index/orientation hypothesis itself is wrong and the search must
! move to the PZT4 constants' own values/units next, treating this
! index-convention fix as closed rather than re-litigating it. NOT YET
! RUN -- push to the cluster before the next sbatch submission.
! ============================================================

!
! ============================================================
! HARMONIC DRIVEN-Y CLONE (2026-09-16): PREP7 cloned from the
! cluster-confirmed h1/2h=1/12 OC modal parent (job 2491761).
! Mesh, mm-N-s-tonne, relative permittivity, FIX v6 TB,PIEZ,
! free-free mechanical BC: UNCHANGED. Solution type is NEW
! (ANTYPE,HARMIC, not LANB).
!
! THIS DECK's electrical BC is the DRIVEN problem:
!   inner electrodes (host/piezo interface, z=+-h): VOLT=0
!   outer electrodes (z=+-(h+h1)): D,VOLT,1.0 on every outer node
! Analytic pole 119.047 Hz, zero 119.405 Hz (job 2491920). FE modal
! pair 118.811 / 119.143 Hz. Read the sweep CSV, never .QUEUE_OK.
! ============================================================
!
! ============================================================
! LEVER 9 HARMONIC ADMITTANCE (2026-09-16): PREP7 cloned from
! the confirmed h1/2h=1/12 OC modal parent (job 2491761).
! Mesh/units/TB,PIEZ unchanged. NEW solution type: ANTYPE,
! HARMIC, driven 1 V on the outer bus. h1/2h=1/12 only.
! Analytic pole 119.047 Hz, zero 119.405 Hz (job 2491920).
! FE modal pair 118.811 / 119.143 Hz. Tiny DMPRAT=1e-4.
! PASS: RUN COMPLETED, 0 MAPDL error lines, |Y| peak then
! dip in 118.5-120.2 Hz with dip above peak. Read the CSV,
! never the queue script's own PASS/FAIL label.
! ============================================================
!
! ============================================================
! LEVER 9 v2 (2026-09-16): dump fix of job 2494669. Same mesh,
! HARFRQ, DMPRAT, KEYOPT(1)=1001. Isolated changes: force label
! CHRG (not AMPS), OUTRES,RSOL, CP-master D,VOLT,1. PASS: RUN
! COMPLETED, 0 MAPDL error lines, |Y| peak then dip in
! 118.5-120.2 Hz with dip above peak, 80 Hz and 140 Hz finite
